Subject: [PROPOSAL] client-hmr: handle graph frames — mount/dispose client rows at runtime

Motivation: mygo r7 live rail installs/uninstalls bundle plugins while an
instance is running (host watchUserPatches replays the profile patch layer).
The node half updates the client module graph on such churn, but the
/plugins/events SSE channel only pushes the graph at connect time and the
browser half explicitly no-ops graph frames — so an already-open page only
sees newly live-installed client rows after a full reload. This proposal
makes graph frames carry membership changes end to end:

- node half (packages/client/hmr/src/index.ts): broadcast the fresh graph
  when clientModules.onGraphChanged fires (the connect-time graph push
  stays as the baseline).
- browser half (packages/client/hmr/src/client/index.ts): diff each graph
  frame against the mounted tree — mount added rows with the boot path's
  own verbs (prefetch for factory registration, then loader.create), dispose
  removed rows with reload()'s documented teardown (registry-first, drain
  inertia, clear fiber, remove owned styles) and drop the entry. Shell-own
  entries (modules wrapper, app-shell assembly) never appear in graphs; a
  baseline set seeded from the first frame guarantees the diff only ever
  touches rows that some graph once listed.

Coexistence with rebuilt frames: rebuilt carries content changes (same id,
new rev), graph carries membership changes (id added/removed); both ride
the same serial queue, so a row rebuilt right after a live mount settles
in order. A graph frame whose membership matches the baseline is a no-op
(rev refreshes stay with the rebuilt/reconnect path, unchanged).

Fixed host snapshot: deepseek-harness-public @ 47f9438 (dsh 0.1.0-rc.6,
public npm line). Verified with git apply --check against that snapshot
(check only; never applied — proposal artifact per dsh-dev rules).

